From: codEx Fork Bot <codex-fork-bot@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 23:17:14 +0800
Subject: rewind: confirm destructive restores with a dry-run preview

- Mirrors Claude Code's rewind dialog: restoring files now shows a
  confirmation with a preview of how many files would be restored and
  deleted before anything is applied, and is skipped entirely when
  nothing would change.
- "Files and conversation" forks only after the preview is confirmed;
  when no matching snapshot exists the conversation still rewinds
  without touching files, matching Claude Code's behavior.
- The Files-only picker asks for confirmation before restoring; restore
  remains refused while a task is running.
- Adds preview_restore with regression tests for changed/new files,
  unchanged workspaces, and missing snapshots, plus an end-to-end
  confirmation-flow test.
